        "title": "08 - Layout and Readability",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Typography at the character level (which typeface, which weight) is only half the problem. Typography at the layout level — how text is arranged in space — determines whether that beautiful typeface is actually readable. Most readability failures in software interfaces are layout failures, not typeface failures."
    },
