        "title": "08 - Layout and Readability",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BRINGHURST'S RULE (Robert Bringhurst, \"The Elements of Typographic Style\"):\n  Optimal measure: 45–75 characters per line (including spaces)\n  For single-column text: 66 characters is widely cited as ideal\n  For multi-column layouts: 40–50 characters per column\n  For footnotes/marginal text: 35–40 characters"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-LAYOUT-READABILITY.md#023",
      "path": [
        "08-LAYOUT-READABILITY.md"
